<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Mesoamerica and the Caribbean</p><h1 class="st-title">Federation of Central America (1921-1922)</h1><p class="st-meta">1921 CE – 1922 CE · capital Tegucigalpa</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Short-lived union of Guatemala, El Salvador and Honduras proclaimed for the centenary of independence in 1921, which fell apart within months.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>For the hundredth anniversary of independence, delegates of the five Central American states signed a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pact-of-union-1921">Pact of Union</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/san-jose-costa-rica">San José</a> in January 1921. <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/republic-of-costa-rica">Costa Rica</a> did not ratify it and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-nicaragua">Nicaragua</a> withdrew, but <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-guatemala">Guatemala</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-el-salvador">El Salvador</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-honduras">Honduras</a> went ahead, and a constituent assembly in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tegucigalpa">Tegucigalpa</a> adopted a federal constitution in September 1921.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The constitution provided for a federal council, congress and courts, with the member states keeping control of most domestic affairs. A provisional federal council met in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tegucigalpa">Tegucigalpa</a> while institutions were set up, but the new federation had little money or authority, and member governments were wary of surrendering power.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In December 1921 a coup in <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-guatemala">Guatemala</a> brought General <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jose-maria-orellana">José María Orellana</a> to power, and in January 1922 he withdrew <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guatemala">Guatemala</a> from the federation. <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-el-salvador">El Salvador</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-honduras">Honduras</a> followed, and the federation dissolved in early 1922. It was the last formal attempt at Central American political union.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="republic, 1921 CE – 1922 CE"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 38 L50 20 L80 38 Z"/><path d="M24 42 H76 M24 80 H76"/><path d="M30 44 V78 M43 44 V78 M57 44 V78 M70 44 V78"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">republic</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Mesoamerica and the Caribbean</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:97.93%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1921 CE – 1922 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Tegucigalpa</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholicism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Spanish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/guatemala">Guatemala</a>, <a href="/countries/el-salvador">El Salvador</a>, <a href="/countries/honduras">Honduras</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Federation of Central America</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1922&amp;focus=federation-of-central-america-1921-1922" aria-label="Federation of Central America (1921-1922) on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="2293 1652 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Federation of Central America (1921-1922) lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M2613 1908L2525 1889M2613 1908L2556 1924M2613 1908L2626 1889"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M2525 1889h0M2556 1924h0M2626 1889h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M2613 1908h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M2613 1908h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Tegucigalpa. <a href="/atlas?year=1922&amp;focus=federation-of-central-america-1921-1922">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

